<title>POLAND: Poland to offer PLN 1.4 bln one-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Poland to offer PLN 1.4 bln one-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury said on Monday it would offer 1.4 billion zlotys of one-year floating bonds in four tranches ending in February 1998.</p>
<p>The coupon of the one-year paper is based on the 12 month inflation rate from two months before the bond matures.</p>
<p> AMOUNT	  MATURITY	 TENDER DATES</p>
<p> 400 million     June 4, 1998     April 23, 1997 and May 21, 1997</p>
<p> 300 million     Sept 3, 1998     July 30, 1997 and August 27, 1997</p>
<p> 400 million     Dec 3, 1998	October 29, 1997 and Nov 26, 1997</p>
<p> 300 million     March 4, 1999    January 28, 1998 and Feb 25, 1998</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
